WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.009
A runner sheet can tell you what someone can do.

2
00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:18.017
It rarely tells you why they keep doing it when the job turns ugly.

3
00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:27.026
Origin Dossier begins in that gap between numbers and motive.

4
00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:36.035
It turns biography into playable pressure: contacts who expect something, enemies who remember too much, debts that pull at the wrong moment, and scars that still shape the next decision.

5
00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:45.044
The goal is not to replace the player.

6
00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:54.052
It is to give the player sharper material to approve, reject, and bring to the table with confidence.

7
00:00:54.052 --> 00:01:03.061
When the GM needs a hook, the dossier should already know which thread has emotional weight.

8
00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:12.070
When the crew needs a reason to care, the past can answer without becoming a lecture.

9
00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:21.078
A good origin does not trap the runner in backstory. It gives the campaign handles.

10
00:01:21.078 --> 00:01:30.087
Origin Dossier makes those handles clear, useful, and ready for trouble.
